About WPP

WPP is the trusted growth partner for the world’s leading brands. We unite&nbsp;cutting-edge media intelligence and data solutions, world-class creativity, next-generation production, transformative enterprise solutions and expert strategic counsel&nbsp;in a single company -&nbsp;powered by exceptional talent and our agentic marketing platform, WPP Open,&nbsp;to help our clients navigate change, capture opportunity and deliver transformational growth. For more information, visit&nbsp; WPP.com .

&nbsp;

What you’ll do &nbsp;

Role Overview &nbsp;

As part of the Global Brand Performance team, the Senior Manager - Brand Performance | Brand-Business Case Modelling &amp; Valuation leads consulting engagements that show how brand affects business performance and value. Financial modelling, brand valuation and intangible-asset analysis are their tools. The role is about helping clients understand how brand can affect growth, demand, pricing power, revenue, margin, cash flow, risk and investment decisions. Working with a broader Landor team, the Senior Manager brings together brand, customer, market and financial evidence to build credible business cases and advise senior stakeholders. &nbsp;

Job Responsibilities &nbsp;

• Leads business/financial focused consulting engagements end-to-end with autonomy: owns scope, hypotheses, workplan, team and partner coordination, quality and delivery, and knows when to involve senior leadership.

• Starts with the strategic and commercial question, then chooses the modelling, valuation and evidence needed to answer it credibly.

• Builds transparent business cases and scenarios that connect brand strength and customer behaviour to commercial and financial outcomes.

• Applies valuation and intangible-asset methods to real decisions, including brand architecture, portfolio optimisation , rebranding, M&amp;A, market entry and marketing investment.

• Brings together brand, customer, market, competitor and financial evidence, making assumptions, sensitivities and limitations clear.

• Turns the analysis into a clear executive story and practical recommendations.

• Leads client conversations and presentations with senior stakeholders, building confidence and buy-in.

• Develops KPI and measurement frameworks that link brand and marketing activity to the business outcomes that matter to the client.

• Works as one Landor team with Strategy, Design, Experience/Innovation and Client Services, and with the global Brand Performance network, sharing methods, tools and learning.

• Contributes to business development and to Landor’s Brand-Business Case Modelling &amp; Valuation offer: pitches, scopes and fees, reusable methods, benchmarks and thought leadership.

• Coaches junior colleagues and sets a high bar for quality and craft at every client touchpoint.

What you’ll need

